    {
      "id": "53e5b58bdedd5c4987300475612abc0d7bff6d7a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1095954919,
          "type": null,
          "body": "So what is the purpose of that field?\n\nIt wasn't showing the protocol, it was showing the name of the dissector, which, as noted in !8100, is not always a protocol name.\n\nI've changed it to show the long name of the protocol.  If the short name is more appropriate, it should call the routine to fetch the short name instead of the long name.  If the dissector name is what was intended, the call should be changed *and* the text and field name should be changed to reflect that it's a dissector name, not a protocol name.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-09-11T08:50:19.477Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-09-11T08:50:19.477Z",
          "system": false,
